Simon's mother was sick in bed. She had a fever. They told Jesus about her.
He helped her. He pulled her hand and helped her stand up. The heat was overwhelming for her. Then she started working on them.
In the evening, after sunset, the people brought to Jesus all the sick. They also brought all those who were possessed by demons.
Everyone in the city gathered in front of the door.
Jesus healed many of them. They had all kinds of diseases. And he also cast out many demons. But he did not let the demons speak, because they knew who he was. Jesus prays in a quiet place.
It was very early in the morning and still dark. Jesus got up and went out of the house. He went to a place where he could be alone. There he prayed.
Simon and his friends went to look for Jesus.
When they found him, they called out to him, "Everyone is looking for you!"
Jesus replied, "Let's go to another place. I want to go to the nearby towns. I must preach there as well. For this I have come."
He walked throughout Galilee. He was preaching in their temples. He also cast out demons. Jesus heals a man who had a skin disease.
A man who had a skin disease came to Jesus. On his knees he begged Jesus. He said, "If you are willing to cleanse me, you can do it."
Jesus was filled with profound anxiety. He reached out and touched the man. "I am willing to do it," he said. "Be cleansed!"
The illness made him disown (his family/relatives).
Jesus immediately drove him out and gave the man a strong warning.
"Don't say that to anyone," he said. "Go and show yourself to the priest. Make the offerings that Moses commanded. You will be a testimony to the priest and to the people that you are 'pure'."
As for the man, he went out and began to tell it immediately. He spread the news to all the people. That's why Jesus could no longer enter the city openly. He used to sit outside in lonely places. But the people were still coming to him from all over.
Jesus heals a man who could not walk.
After a few days, Jesus returned to Capernaum. The people heard that he had returned home.
A large crowd gathered, so that there was no room left. There was not even any room outside the door. But Jesus preached to them the word.
Four of those who came were carrying a man who could not walk.
What they couldn't approach to Jesus because of the crowd. They made a hole in the ceiling above Jesus. And after that, they lowered the man through it onto a mat.
Jesus saw their faith. He said to the man, "Child, your sins are forgiven."
Some teachers of the law were sitting there, reasoning to themselves,
Why does this man speak like this? He is saying something very evil! Only God can forgive sins!
Jesus knew what they were thinking. He said to them, "Why do you think about these things?"
Is it easier to say to the man, "Your sins are forgiven"? Or to say, "Get up, take your bed and walk"?
"We love you to know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins." Then Jesus spoke again to the man who could not walk.
"I tell you," he said, "get up. Take your belongings and go back to your home."
The man stood up and took his mat. Then he went out, and everyone marveled at him. Everyone was astonished, and they glorified God, saying, "We have never seen anything like this!" Jesus Chooses Levi
Again Jesus went out beside the Sea of Galilee. A great crowd came to him. He began to teach them.
As he was going, he saw Levi, the son of Alphaeus. Levi was sitting in the tax collector's booth. "Follow me," Jesus told him. Levi got up and followed him.
Later, Jesus was having dinner at Levi's house. Many tax collectors and "sinners" were eating with him and his disciples. They were part of the large crowd that followed Jesus.
There were some teachers of the law who were Pharisees. They saw Jesus eating with "sinners" and tax collectors. So they asked his disciples, "Why does he eat with tax collectors and 'sinners'?"
Jesus heard this. And he said to them, "Those who are in good health do not need a physician; but those who are sick do need one. I did not come to call the righteous, but sinners." They asked Jesus about fasting.
The disciples of John and the Pharisees do not eat. People came to Jesus. They said to him, "The disciples of John fast, and the disciples of the Pharisees also fast. But your disciples do not fast. Why do your disciples not fast?"
Jesus answered, "How can the guests of the bridegroom fast while he is with them? They cannot fast as long as he is with them.
The time will come when the bridegroom is taken from them. On that day, they will leave without eating.
People don't sew a new piece of cloth onto old clothing. If they did, the new piece would tear away from the old. This would cause the tear to get worse.
People don't put new wine into old wine skins. If they do, the wine will burst the skins. Then the wine and the skins will all be ruined. No, everyone puts new wine into new skins." Jesus is Lord of the Sabbath
On the Sabbath, Jesus was walking with His disciples in the grain fields. The disciples began to pluck some grain heads.
The Pharisees said to Jesus, "Look, this man is breaking the law by healing on the Sabbath."
Answer, "Have you never read about what David did? He and his men were hungry. They needed food."
During that time, Abiathar was the high priest. David entered the house of God and ate the holy bread. Only the priests were allowed to eat it. David also gave some to his men.
Then Jesus said to them, "The Sabbath was made for man. Man was not made for the Sabbath.
So the Son of Man is Lord even of the Sabbath.
Healing on the Sabbath.
Again Jesus went to the synagogue. There was a man whose hand was weak and deformed.
There were some Pharisees who were trying to find fault with Jesus. They were watching him closely. They wanted to see if he would heal the man on the Sabbath day.
Jesus spoke to the man who had a withered and crooked hand. He said to him, "Stand in front of everyone."
Jesus asked them, "What does the law say one must do on the Sabbath? To do good or to do evil? To save life or to destroy it?" But no one answered him.
Jesus looked at them with anger. He was very upset because their hearts were hardened. Then He said to the man, "Stretch out your hand." He stretched it out, and his hand was restored as new.
Afterward, the Pharisees went out and began to plot with the Herodians against Jesus, hoping to kill him. The crowds follow Jesus.
Jesus walked by the Sea of Galilee with his disciples. A great crowd from Galilee followed him.
The people heard about all the things Jesus was doing. And they came to him in great numbers. They came from Judea, Jerusalem, and Idumea. They came from the territories east of the Jordan River. And they came from the region around Tyre and Sidon.
Because of the crowd, Jesus told his disciples to bring him a small boat. This was to prevent people from crowding him.
Jesus healed many people. Therefore, those who were sick were pushing themselves to touch him.
When the people who had evil spirits saw him, they fell down before him. The spirits cried out, "You are the Son of God!"
But Jesus commanded them not to tell who he was. Jesus appoints the twelve apostles.
Jesus went up on a mountain. He called certain people to come to Him, and they came.
He appointed 12 of them and called them apostles. They have been with him ever since. He also used to send them out to preach.
They had the authority to cast out demons.
Jesus appointed the twelve. Simon was one of them. Jesus gave him the name Peter.
They were James, the son of Zebedee, and his brother John. Jesus gave them the name Boanerges. Boanerges means Sons of Thunder.
They were also Andrew, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, and James the son of Alphaeus. And they were also Thaddaeus and Simon the Zealot.
Judas Iscariot was one of them too. He was the one who would later betray Jesus to his enemies. Jesus and Beelzebub
Jesus entered a house. Once again a crowd gathered. It was so large that Jesus and his disciples couldn't even eat.
His family heard about this. They went to take care of him. They said, "He is crazy."
Some teachers of the law were there. They had come down from Jerusalem. They said, "He is controlled by Beelzebul! He drives out demons by the power of the prince of demons."
Jesus called them, sat down to talk with them in parables. He said to them, "How can Satan cast out Satan?"
If a kingdom is at war within its own spirit, it cannot endure.
If the family is divided, it cannot survive.
